    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate variability",
    "problem": "Forecasting decadal climate fluctuations is challenging because the coupled ocean-atmosphere mechanisms are poorly understood, particularly how propagating sea-surface temperature anomalies create a predictable atmospheric response and feedback cycle.",
    "method": "We propose a mechanism for forecasting decadal climate variability based on a coupled ocean-atmosphere feedback loop, where the advective propagation of sea-surface-temperature anomalies across the North Atlantic creates a predictable, recurring cycle.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze shipboard observations to demonstrate the decadal predictability of North Atlantic sea surface temperature, arising from the advective propagation of anomalies and a potential coupled ocean-atmosphere mechanism.",
